SUMMARY:Mental Health First Aid Training
DESCRIPTION:Mental Health First Aid (MHFA) is an early intervention public 
 education program. It teaches adults how to recognize the signs and 
 symptoms that suggest a potential mental health challenge\, how to listen 
 nonjudgmentally and give reassurance to a person who may be experiencing a 
 mental health challenge\, and how to refer a person to appropriate 
 professional support and services.\n\n \n\nThe Mental Health Association's 
 Intensive Family Support Services(IFSS) provides support to family members 
 of adults living with mental health conditions. IFSS staff\, Eileen 
 Strungis and Mel Bryan\, will be offering an in-person course Monday\, 
 April 27th\, from 10:00am-5:00pm at the Montclair Public Library.  
 Workbooks covering the material and lunch will be provided for all 
 attendees. There is no cost to participate\, but seats are limited. \n\n 
 \n\nIf you would like to join us for this interactive\, evidence-based 
 course to learn valuable skills to assist those living with mental health 
 challenges\, please reach out to Eileen at estrungis@mhainspire.org\, or 
 reply to this email for next steps.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Outside Organization
UID:LibCal-10306-16585774
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16585774
