SUMMARY:Microsoft Excel I
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\n\nExcel is Microsoft 365 software that organizes and analyzes 
 information in spreadsheet format. It has a wide array of tools for data 
 analysis.  Excel provides options for presenting complex data via charts 
 and graphs.\n\nThe class is geared to beginners and those who seek a 
 refresher in the topic.  Students will gain a basic understanding of the 
 worksheet environment\, tools for working with data\, and resources for 
 continued learning.\n\nWhat you will learn\nWorksheet basics with budget 
 practice worksheet - Learn elements of the worksheet\, enter and edit 
 budget data\, perform calculations\, create a pie chart.\n\nImportant 
 Note\nThis is a hands-on class\; students should have ability to use the 
 mouse and keyboard.  Students are welcome to bring a flash drive to save 
 their work for review and practice.\n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Classroom\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School
UID:LibCal-10306-16359538
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16359538
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260502T151500Z
DTEND:20260502T161500Z
DTSTAMP:20260502T000000Z
SUMMARY:Open Book\, Open Mind\; Daniel Okrent\, "Art Ain't Easy"
DESCRIPTION:Daniel Okrent\, a distinguished journalist and author\, talks 
 with Alexandra Jacobs of The New York Times Book Review about the complex 
 inner world of one of the 20th century’s most beloved theatrical 
 composers. Part of Yale University Press's Jewish Lives series. " I have 
 had the same conversation with three musical theater fan friends\, where we 
 started out wondering what else we needed to know about Sondheim but found 
 Okrent’s book a marvelous feast full of new insights. And if you’re a 
 newbie\, Okrent’s book is a great place to begin. As Noël Coward put it 
 in his delightful 'I Went to a Marvelous Party\,' I couldn’t have liked 
 it more."―John McWhorter\, The New York Times\n\nPresented in 
 collaboration with the Montclair Literary Festival. No registration 
 required. \n\nThe discussion will be followed by an audience Q&A and book 
 sales and signing with Watchung Booksellers. \n\nOpen Book / Open Mind is 
 sponsored by Montclair Public Library Foundation\, Watchung Booksellers\, 
 Anonymous\, David and Mary Lee Jones\, and our individual Underwriters. We 
 are also grateful for the generous support of our in-kind sponsors\, First 
 Congregational Church of Montclair\, The George\, and Amanti Vino. To 
 support Open Book / Open Mind and other library programs\, click here to 
 donate.
LOCATION:Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Open Book / Open Mind
UID:LibCal-10306-16726805
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16726805
END:VEVENT
