DTSTART:20260512T171500Z
DTEND:20260512T181500Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T000000Z
SUMMARY:Everything Book Club\, "A Rising Man" by Abir Mukherjee
DESCRIPTION:Winner of CWA Dagger Award. A richly atmospheric\, twisting 
 "mystorical" set in Calcutta\, 1919. The body of a senior official has been 
 found in a filthy sewer\, and a note left in his mouth warns the British to 
 quit India\, or else. Captain Sam Wyndham\, former Scotland Yard 
 detective\, and Sergeant Banerjee\, one of the few Indians to be recruited 
 into the new CID—embark on an investigation that will take them from the 
 mansions of British traders to the opium dens of the city. Perfect for AAPI 
 Heritage Month! \n\n“An enthralling debut.”—The New York 
 Times\n\nAbir Mukherjee is the child of immigrants from India who grew up 
 in Scotland. After 20 years of working as an accounted\, he started writing 
 crime fiction. "A Rising Man" is his debut novel. Mukherjee lives near 
 London. \n\n \n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Tower Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Book Discussion
UID:LibCal-10306-15933640
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/15933640
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260512T173000Z
DTEND:20260512T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T000000Z
SUMMARY:How to Retire to the Caribbean Through Investment Online NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nAre you dreaming of a morning smoothie on the pink sand 
 beaches of Bermuda or a leisurely afternoon snorkel session by the glorious 
 barrier reef near Belize? In this free talk\, Hoda Elamir\, an attorney who 
 specializes in advising clients on how to retire to the Caribbean through 
 investments\, the most popular method\, will explain the how it works and 
 answer questions. The class explores global mobility\, 
 citizenship-by-investment\, and retiring abroad. It examines how 
 individuals and families can leverage cross-border residency and 
 citizenship programs for asset protection\, tax optimization\, and 
 lifestyle planning.
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School
UID:LibCal-10306-16406946
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16406946
