SUMMARY:Free Live Klezmer Concert with Midnight Nosh
DESCRIPTION:This is a free Adult School class. Click below to 
 register.\n\nJoin us for an spirited\, exciting performance by Midnight 
 Nosh\, a five-piece band of piano/accordion\, sax\, bass\, guitar\, and 
 drums\, led by Rabbi Daniel Brenner. Klezmer\, a traditional musical art 
 form of of Eastern European Jews\, includes dance tunes\, ritual melodies\, 
 and virtuosic improvisations played at weddings and other social functions. 
 It's almost impossible not to dance to the free-wheeling strains of klezmer 
 so wear your comfortable shoes. Rabbi Brenner will teach everyone classic 
 klezmer dance moves and hand motions. Families welcome.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Music
