DTSTAMP:20260527T000000Z
SUMMARY:5K Training - No Boundaries
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class.\n\nClick here to register 
 for the early bird price\, available until April 3rd.\n\nClick here for 
 registrations April 3rd and later.\n\nHave you always wanted to run or walk 
 a 5K but didn't know how to begin training? Maybe you are nervous or don't 
 want to do it alone? Maybe you have had a hard time sticking to a training 
 program in the past? If you answered "Yes" to any of the above\, our iconic 
 beginner program is perfect for you. Often the first step is the 
 hardest.\n\nThe camaraderie of a group and experience of your coaches and 
 mentors provide great support toward healthier habits and lifestyle. This 
 program is designed for people just starting a walking/running routine for 
 the first time\, restarting after a winter hiatus and those who want to run 
 faster or longer. In 8 weeks\, meeting twice a week\, our fun\, 
 unintimidating program will help you walk\, walk-run or run across the 
 finish line at the Fitzgerald 5k Lager Run in June.\n\nIn collaboration 
 with Dawn and John Fabbro of Fleet Feet Montclair.\n
LOCATION:Montclair - Anderson Park\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School
UID:LibCal-10306-15827869
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/15827869
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260527T223000Z
DTEND:20260528T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260527T000000Z
SUMMARY:Home Repair Essentials NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to register. 
 \n\nLearn the fundamentals of home repair in this practical\, hands-on 
 workshop taught by Robert Haas\, instructor of the popular Woodworking 101 
 and Advanced Woodworking classes. Held at Montclair High School\, this 
 course gives participants a behind-the-walls look at how common home 
 features are built and maintained.\n\nDuring the class\, Robert will 
 construct two demonstration walls that include doors and a window\, showing 
 how these elements are installed and how typical wall structures are 
 assembled. Participants will also learn how traditional double-hung windows 
 operate and how they can be repaired\, including basic glass pane 
 replacement.\n\nThe workshop will also introduce the basics of residential 
 wiring\, demonstrating how outlets and lighting are installed and 
 connected. Throughout the session\, Robert will answer questions and offer 
 guidance on a wide range of home repair topics.\n\nWhether you're a 
 homeowner looking to handle basic repairs yourself or simply curious about 
 how things in your home work\, this class provides practical knowledge you 
 can use right away.
LOCATION:Montclair - Montclair High School\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Arts & Crafts
UID:LibCal-10306-16878802
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16878802
