SUMMARY:Marcel Duchamp: The Alchemist of the Avant Garde - Online NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\nOpen the dictionary to the word “iconoclast\,” and you will 
 see a picture of Marcel Duchamp. He challenged the standards and beliefs of 
 the art world and ushered in a new era of creative license—the 
 reverberations of which are still felt in contemporary art today. 
 Duchamp’s imagination was aroused by elements of Cubism\, Surrealism\, 
 and even Pop Art\, but his resourcefulness meant continuous 
 self-reinvention and deliberate inconsistency. He once said\, “I have 
 forced myself to contradict myself in order to avoid conforming to my own 
 taste.” Come and learn about his innovative works and the shockwaves they 
 produced. A blockbuster Duchamp retrospective will be up at the Museum of 
 Modern Art from April 12 to August 22.
LOCATION:Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Lectures / History & Culture
UID:LibCal-10306-16492906
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16492906
END:VEVENT
