SUMMARY:[MILL Senior Friday] Lithographic Art Posters with Maggie Rothman
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Fridays for a day full of events for Seniors with 
 the MILL @ MPL! All events are free and open to the public. Registration is 
 recommended unless otherwise noted.\n\n\nDelve into the world of art 
 posters and learn that they were much more than just advertising. From the 
 historically significant propaganda century to contemporary minimalist 
 designs\, learn how art posters impacted the art world as well as society. 
 \n\nHOW TO REGISTER\nThis class is run by the MILL. Please register for 
 classes directly through their website here. This class is offered both 
 in-person and hybrid on Zoom.\n\nFor questions about MILL classes please 
 call 973-744-3278.\n\nMILL @ MPL is made possible through a partnership 
 between the MILL\, Montclair Public Library and Partners for Health.\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Lectures / History & Culture
UID:LibCal-10306-16678841
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16678841
