SUMMARY:Era Uma Vez\, na Biblioteca (Once Upon A Time At The Library): Portuguese Storytime
DESCRIPTION:“Era Uma Vez\, na Biblioteca” (Once Upon a Time\, at the 
 Library) welcomes all families to be part of this experience of 
 storytelling in Portuguese. The stories will be interwoven with little 
 songs and rhymes\, all in Portuguese. The storyteller\, Ana Cristina 
 Coura\, is an educator with a background in psychology who has taught 
 children in Brazil and worked as an art educator. Registration is 
 required.\n\n \n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Children's Programs, Language, Storytime, Special Event, Story Time
UID:LibCal-10306-16730492
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16730492
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260606T190000Z
DTEND:20260606T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260606T000000Z
SUMMARY:Our Journeys: A Storytelling Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an interactive workshop that honors 
 intergenerational storytelling\, preserves community voices\, and connects 
 participants through shared reflections. Through photo prompts participants 
 of all backgrounds will explore ways to document family journeys. A 
 storytelling workbook\, courtesy of Quill Hawk Publishing\, will be given 
 to participants to continue documenting their family stories at home. Free 
 to participate! \n\n\n\n \n\nFacilitator: \nTracey Nguyễn Mang is the 
 founder of nonprofit organization\, Vietnamese Boat People (VBP) and a real 
 estate professional based in Montclair NJ. Inspired by her family’s 
 journey\, she created VBP to preserve the stories of Vietnamese refugees 
 and amplify voices often left out of mainstream narratives. Through 
 storytelling\, she seeks to foster empathy\, bridge generations\, and build 
 understanding across cultures.\n\n\n\nSponsored by: AAPI New Jersey\, Quill 
 Hawk Publishing\n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Local History Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Adult Services, Lectures / History & Culture, Writing
UID:LibCal-10306-16878830
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16878830
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260606T190000Z
DTEND:20260606T203000Z
DTSTAMP:20260606T000000Z
SUMMARY:Shadow Tellers: Shadow-Puppet Story Factory (All ages welcome)
DESCRIPTION:We have been marveling at the stories that emerge between 
 shadow and light since we gathered around the first fire. Let's make 
 shadow-puppet silhouettes! Kids design characters to their hearts' 
 content\, gather around cardboard theater boxes\, and explore stories 
 together. Grownups will enjoy the privilege of helping their kids cut out 
 shadow puppets and being their very first studio audience as children fill 
 the room with the light of their imaginations. Do drop in (no registration 
 required)!\n\n \n\n \n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Storytime Room
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts
UID:LibCal-10306-16922434
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16922434
END:VEVENT
