SUMMARY:The Juneteenth Cookbook: Alliah Agostini - Author Visit & Craft (  Tobias the Horse on the Lawn!)
DESCRIPTION:Alliah Agostini - 4-5 p.m.\n\nProlific Children’s author 
 Alliah L. Agostini reads excerpts from her stunning kids’ recipe book The 
 Juneteenth Cookbook. She’ll go over the importance of African-American 
 culinary traditions and why great cuisine and Juneteenth go hand-in-hand. 
 Afterwards\, kids will make their own 90’s inspired African medallion 
 necklaces - just like in the Juneteenth Cookbook! Registration recommended 
 for reminders and updates. \n\nTobias the Horse also continues his 
 tradition of appearing at annual Juneteenth events. Look for him on the 
 Library lawn (Plymouth Street) and say hello between 3 to 5 pm!\n\n \n\n 
 \n\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10306-16816526
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16816526
